The scoring engine applies an authoritative 8-stage fallback chain (Final -> Management -> Auditor -> HR PMS -> Skip-Level -> Manager -> Self -> 0) when resolving the displayed score for a KPI. The 'Self' tier reads from review_submissions.achieved_value, which is a FROZEN per-submission snapshot — never a live FK to org_kpi_values. Per POLICY §88 (Submission Snapshot Immutability, v2.66.7.3): admin edits to upstream Org KPI sources MUST NOT silently mutate already-approved historical scores. Re-propagation is always an explicit, audit-logged action initiated by Data Owner or Admin. Any refactor replacing review_submissions value columns with live FK lookups is forbidden — it would violate HR audit law and final-score immutability governance.
